From d2207e51a4430aea68aefbc00f92ec2ff5da971e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrice Brissette <pbrisset@cisco.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:14:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 122/123] bgpd,zebra,lib,tools: EVPN L3 multihoming without an
 L2VNI

Squashed backport of the FRRouting/frr#23304 EVPN L3MH series to FRR
10.7.1. The bgp_evpn_l3mh topotest is in the next patch.

"advertise-all-vni l3vni-neigh" under address-family l2vpn evpn lets EVPN
multihomed leaves sync host ARP/ND entries to their ES peers when the
VLAN has only an L3VNI. A local neighbor on an ES access port is
advertised as a pure-L3 RT-2: label[0] = Explicit NULL, label[1] = L3VNI,
ESI = the host's ES. An ES peer that receives it installs the host as an
extern_learn neighbor on its SVI, with a static sync-MAC FDB entry on the
ES bond. No L2VNI is needed.

Included:
- the knob, frr-reload support, show fields and
  "debug bgp|zebra evpn mh l3vni-neigh";
- ETAG in the MAC/IP ZAPI message, and the L3MH sync flag;
- ES base-EVPN and originator IP sourced from the L3VNI;
- pure-L3 RT-2 originate, receive and install, with ESI resolution and
  re-install after a kernel flush;
- L2VNI add/remove handoff, and host mobility;
- bgpd: free residual ES-VTEPs on ES teardown;
- zebra: withdraw EVPN routes before VNI delete;
- review fixes: ETAG-selected SVI must be in the L3VNI's VRF; a local
  learn on the synced SVI keeps the kernel entry; synced neighbors follow
  VRF import-RT changes; local routes follow VRF RD and export-RT changes;
  local routes are withdrawn when the L3VNI goes down; IPv6 link-local
  neighbors are not synced; a local delete falls back to the peer's
  sync; a peer's ADD is held while the VLAN has an L2VNI; a local learn
  over a synced entry keeps the MAC->port binding and its ESI.

Changes from FRR master, needed for 10.7.1:
- bgp_evpn.c: the pure-L3 checks are placed in the 10.7.1 import-RT
  lookup (lookup_import_rt/lookup_vrf_import_rt).
- bgp_evpn_vty.c: the advertise-all-vni commands become DEFPY, and the
  show field is added to the 10.7.1 display_l3vni().

Tested with the bgp_evpn_l3mh topotest from FRRouting/frr#23304 on 10.7.1
with the full SONiC patch series: 41 passed.

Signed-off-by: Patrice Brissette <pbrisset@cisco.com>
